# crontab -e, with <checkout> replaced by the path to this repository's
# checkout. The watchdog keeps the current run alive (a host restart kills
# every process); the refresh builds PostgreSQL master's newest commit
# nightly and, when ephyra-postgresql's tests pass on it, moves the run to
# it; pre-triage judges new findings.
@reboot     <checkout>/case-studies/postgresql/coverage/deploy/watchdog.sh
*/5 * * * * <checkout>/case-studies/postgresql/coverage/deploy/watchdog.sh
30 5 * * *  <checkout>/case-studies/postgresql/coverage/deploy/refresh-master.sh
*/30 * * * * <checkout>/case-studies/postgresql/coverage/deploy/pretriage.sh
